WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.131 --> 00:00:00.964
(playful music)

00:00:00.964 --> 00:00:01.890
- [Narrator] Chicken.

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:06.450
You can eat it for breakfast,
lunch, dinner and dessert.

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:08.373
Yes, I said dessert.

00:00:16.872 --> 00:00:20.372
(speaks foreign language)

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:27.080
Mahmut is the manager, master chef,

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:30.660
and second generation owner
of this charming pudding shop.

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:33.610
One of the puddings they
specialize in, is tavuk göğsü.

00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:36.083
Also known as chicken breast pudding.

00:00:36.956 --> 00:00:40.456
(speaks foreign language)

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:58.910
Intricate it is.

00:00:58.910 --> 00:01:01.220
Step one: Boil chicken just enough

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:04.620
to take apart the white meat.
And then, move on to step two:

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:07.860
Mix water buffalo milk with
some cow's milk like you do,

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:08.880
and get them boiling.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:11.660
Once that boils, you can
move onto step three:

00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:14.040
Add in some broken rice,
and once that starches

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.710
mix with that water buffalo milk,

00:01:15.710 --> 00:01:17.520
you've got yourself an emulsifier.

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:21.014
And that, my friends, is
how you make tavuk göğsü.

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:24.514
(speaks foreign language)

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:34.420
Nutritious?

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:35.705
Check.

00:01:35.705 --> 00:01:36.920
Amazing flavor? Check, check.

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:38.943
And the people of Turkey really love it.

00:01:39.988 --> 00:01:43.488
(speaks foreign language)

00:02:06.335 --> 00:02:09.002
(playful music)

